      {
        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "Deepen: choosing one or two words",
        "body": "¿Qué aprendiste ayer sobre esta misma materia?\n\nEscribe aquí:\n____________________\n____________________\n____________________\n\n## Repaso\n\nDeepen: two-word times.\n\nWe worked the two-word path: helper haber + participle (-ado/-ido), with he cantado, había canta\n\nExplain one idea with your own words.\n\nToday we put the whole week into one skill: **choosing**. You are the guide. First listen to what the sentence wants to say; then pick one word or two. We are not memorizing rare grammar names—we are learning to hear the sentence and decide. Your ear plus a time clue beats guessing from the first verb shape you remember. Ask three questions in order. Is there a closed moment like «yesterday at five»? → usually **one word** (canté). Does the result still matter now («already», «this week»)? → often **two words** (he cantado). Is it background or past habit? → imperfect **one word** (cantaba). Ask them one after another until the sentence feels right. Hear three mini-stories: «Terminé ayer» closes the past; «He terminado ya» keeps the result alive; «Leía cuando llamaron» paints background then a closed hit.\n\nMira este ejemplo. Look at this example. Say one sentence about what you learned.\n\nPractice: Now it's your turn. Práctica: Ahora te toca a ti. Draw one clear symbol or small scene about “Choose one word or two”. Add one label from today's lesson.\n\nCommon mistake: Error común:\n\n## Drawing for the image band\nDraw one clear symbol or small scene about “Choose one word or two”. Add one label from today's lesson."
      }
    ],
